Roundup (3 rounds, honest):
R1  FAILED — raced the initial discovery sweep (CLI calls landed before the
    first Refresh finished; "no board matches"). Fixed the smoke to poll.
R2  FAILED — controller slot held the whole run (eval/audit stuck as
    observer). Two findings:
    (a) PRE-EXISTING zombie: an earlier T8/T10 HIL connection died without
        FIN (the documented net-down FIN-miss, §13); board-side keepalive
        did not reap it. Operator recovery per ErrControllerSlotHeld's
        ruling: USB CDC open = reboot (§2) into a clean arbitration table.
    (b) MY OWN recovery probe then re-created the zombie: CDC has NO host
        disconnect signal (§12 — slot held until reboot or YIELD). The
        correct recovery is hello(controller) → hello{observer:true} 讓位
        → close. Verified: yield releases the slot.
    (c) DAEMON BUG (fixed): startupAudit called sup.Resync directly,
        bypassing daemonBoard.connectMu — audit racing a request-path
        connect double-dialed the board into two controller connections;
        §12 forces the loser observer with no preemption (self-inflicted
        slot_held). All supervisor-touching paths (audit / board_status
        ScriptList / lease teardown / request ops) now serialize under
        connectMu.
R3  PASS — full flow below (serve → list → status → lease → eval value face
    → eval out face → eval error face → repl one line → release → SIGINT
    graceful: sock removed, teardown err=<nil> 18ms, no leftover state).

